(ROOT/'artifact.md').write_text('''# Manuscript reference contract\n\nDesign authorities: LMS FINAL.pdf and FORMAT-FOR-MANUSCRIPT (2).pdf. Authoring source: LMS FINAL (1).docx. Only Chapters 1–3, the supplied title page, and their references are in scope. No fabricated approval sheet, abstract, results, signatures, or sample counts.\n\nUse the exact required heading order: Chapter 1 sections 1.1–1.9; Chapter 2 related studies, related systems, synthesis, research gap; Chapter 3 sections 3.1 Research Design, 3.2 System and Project Overview, 3.3 Respondents, 3.4 Sampling Technique, 3.5 Instruments and Methods for Data Collection, 3.6 Hardware Requirements, 3.7 Software Requirements, 3.8 Flowchart, 3.9 Entity Relationship Diagram, 3.10 Data Flow Diagram. Additional methodology content stays under 3.5.\n\nPreserve the source PDF's 8.5×13 portrait pages, Times New Roman 12-point justified body, half-inch first-line indent and double spacing. Match the PDF body starting around 122 points; retain source left/right/bottom margins and cover arrangement. Reuse the original branded header as a high-resolution image to retain its exact blackletter appearance and logos, with its decorative line. Original footer art remains. Preserve original title wording and date, with a date-confirmation comment.\n\nRetain the six named feature categories required by the format guide. Only Students and Instructors are respondents; two role-specific questionnaires. Technical testing is conducted by the researchers, and instrument validation is separate. No expert respondent sample. Reverse pyramid background names identifiable international universities first, Philippine institutions next, and CdM ICS last.\n\nRebuild inaccurate diagrams. Flowcharts use terminators, I/O parallelograms, processes, decisions, predefined processes, matched on-page circles and off-page pentagons. Separate overview, authentication/registration and enrollment details. Provide visible arrowheads, branch labels, orthogonal routing, connector key, and editable diagrams.net source. ERDs use schema-derived entity names, explicit cardinalities and selected fields; proposed extension uses dashed outlines. DFDs use labelled directional data flows, proper entities/processes/stores, and existing/proposed status explanations.\n\nAPA 7 bibliography: retain only cited sources and verified author/year/DOI records; alphabetical order, hanging indent, italic titles/venues where required. Validate comments, XML, unchanged original hashes, heading order, survey groups, diagram linkage, and all rendered pages before delivery.\n''',encoding='utf-8')
print('Content and fidelity contract prepared')
